  "reason": "Evidence: config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) is the clear best at 0.619 acc, showing that multiprofile+avgpool aggregation is the dominant design choice. However, fusion method has only been tested as concat; we have no data on whether learned weighted fusion could better balance the RNA and image modalities in this strong setting. Question: config_019 is identical to config_018 except fusion changes from concat to weighted, giving a clean single-variable A/B test. Why best next: it is the lowest-risk, highest-information experiment around the current optimum—confirming or refuting whether concat is already near-optimal for fusion. A positive result opens a new exploitation axis; a negative result efficiently closes the fusion dimension so remaining budget can focus on image encoder (ViT-L) or RNA encoder (scvi/scgpt) upgrades."
}

